If your application depends on the layered products that you have listed above,
then THEY would all need to be available and stable before you could migrate
to an Alpha AXP environment. So that (second guessing) may be what your sales
rep. was referring to.

The OS itself (OpenVMS AXP) is "production quality" today. However, you also
need to keep your dependencies on other products and capabilities in mind
before deciding that the OpenVMS AXP system would be a suitable environment
for your application today.

If you have the goal of moving to the Alpha AXP environment, then I'm sure
your sales rep will be happy to help you plan the transition as soon as
you are able, and can help you maximise your investment protection, buy
selling you "Alpha Ready" systems today, so your peripherals, boxes,
software etc. can be transferred to the new system when you are ready.


