I just tested the memory usage of a monochrome VXT2000 with 16Mb RAM by 
starting the memory-meter and then logging into a DECstation 5000/200 by xdm. 
I used mwm (1.1.3) as supplied by DEC. After logging in and starting the screen
clock, session manager, xconsole and one dxterm I had 7828 Mb free.
I then loaded a gif picture onto the root with xv, and went down to 7634 Mb 
free. As a further test I started 4 dxterms, one xterm, xdvi and ghostscript
simultaneously and ended up with 7268 Mb free. All this should have worked
on a 12 Mb box too. There is no problem at all with the response either, though
the local window manager is slightly faster than using a remote manager. Are you
sure that the terminals are correctly configured and that they are running
the 1.1 version of the VXT software? My box get all its fonts by LAT, perhaps
TFTP uses more memory?

As you can guess I am happy with the hardware and software. Less so with the
way DEC sold me the thing - somehow they forgot to mention one needs an 
expansion board for memory above 4 Mb, not just the memory itself... We had to
pay extra to get that though the box was sold as a "complete".

-psi 

