In article <28OCT199217435884@csa2.lbl.gov> tonse@csa2.lbl.gov (S R Tonse (510)-486-6349) writes:
>Dear All, I use a DecStation 5000, running Ultrix 4.1. I have been trying
>to install a new SCSI disk, a Micropolis 1528 with the following specs:
>
>1531.1 Mbytes (1342.3 Mbytes when formatted)

You'll need to upgrade to Ultrix 4.2 or greater to make full use of your
disk.  Ultrix 4.1 does not handle disks above ~1.2gb.

From the Ultrix FAQ (which hasn't been posted recently):

==============================================
19. Why doesn't ULTRIX 4.1 work with disks bigger than 1.2GBytes?

There is a bug in the V4.1 SCSI driver that will only allow it to read
something like (2 ** 21) or (2 ** 20) LBNs.  After that it wraps
around to the beginning of the disk.  It is fixed in V4.2.

